{title: Joy Comes in the Morning}
{subtitle: Psalms 30:5–6}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm7] |
| [Cm7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I was [Eb]lifted from the deep place
You did [Cm7]not let them gloat
I cried [Ab]out for your help
And you [Bb]healed my broken soul
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You [Eb]brought me from the dead
Kept me alive from [Cm7]the pit
I stand here by your [Ab]grace
Your mercy is my on[Bb]ly light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sing to the Lord his [Eb]faithful ones
Give thanks [Bb]to his [Cm7]holy [Ab]name
His [Eb]anger lasts [Bb]but a [Cm7]moment
His favor a life[Bb]time
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Ab/Bb]Weeping [Ab]may spend the [Eb]night [Ebmaj7/D]
[Cm7]But joy comes in the morn[Bb/D]ing
[Eb]The darkness fades away
When [Ab]the light starts returning
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sing to [Bb]the Lord his faithful ones
[Eb]Give thanks to his ho[Bb]ly name
[Cm7]His an[Ab]ger lasts [Eb]but a mo[Bb]ment
His [Cm7]favor a lifetime
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
When I [Bb]felt [Ab]secure I [Eb]said [Bb/D][Cm7][Bb/D][Eb][Abmaj7][Bb]
I [Eb]would never be shaken
But [Cm7]when you hid your face
[Ab]My heart was filled with [Bb]terror
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Joy comes in [Eb]the morn[Bb]ing
[Cm7]Joy comes in [Eb]the morn[Bb][Cm7]ing
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
